Subject: [PATCH 0002/0012] give the streamer a frame the compositor can import

The decoder hands out DMA-BUF backed NV12 frames, and the interface can only
sample a Vulkan image it owns. This patch adds the three ways the streamer can
bridge that gap and the diagnostics that say which one a session took:

* a CPU copy of the two NV12 planes for the case where the adopted device
  cannot import the decoder's buffer at all;
* a linear NV12 VkBuffer import, so a device that supports the external-buffer
  bit can copy the decoder's planes on the GPU instead of on the CPU;
* a cache keyed by the DMA-BUF object, so the same buffer is imported once and
  then reused frame after frame;
* the frame counter and the first-frame PPM dump that every later measurement
  in this layer quotes.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

